		{
			"id": "109668228352291183",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mstdn.ca/@AmeliasBrain/109668228295715766",
			"author": {
				"name": "Amelia Bellamy-Royds :progress:",
				"url": "https://mstdn.ca/@AmeliasBrain",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/355/151/582/876/743/original/773bd1e4ff2fad73.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-11T02:32:42.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Hmmm... someone mentioned this to me a couple weeks ago (we were talking about how there's no easy recommendation system built into streaming services &amp; I mentioned thinking about starting an alt Twitter account for micro reviews) &amp; I was all \"I dunno if I want a whole other social network...\"</p><p>But if my peeps are already there, that'd be different, yeah?</p><p>You wouldn't happen to be planning a blog post all about what's good/bad/quirky about the service &amp; how to get comfortable quickly?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109668313689782807",
			"parentId": "109668228352291183",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@bkardell/109668313618211877",
			"author": {
				"name": "bkardell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@bkardell",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/565/409/427/409/original/27c5979b96ec51b3.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-11T02:54:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.ca/@AmeliasBrain\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>AmeliasBrain</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> i didn't even know that existed, but would love to read that post if you write it</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109671085446712957",
			"parentId": "109668313689782807",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109671085446712957",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-11T14:39:19.084Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@bkardell\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>bkardell</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.ca/@AmeliasBrain\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>AmeliasBrain</span></a></span> ha! I don’t think I have the time budget to write this post right now—but I will say that I subscribed to pro last night and it has rekindled a sense of community around movies that I had been missing for a long time!</p><p>I think the biggest UX confusions for me are: 1. orthogonal features for “like” and 5-star ratings. 2. Why the Diary is anything but your recent activity? When I rate a movie it doesn’t go into the Diary? I don’t understand why 😅</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109671338329197838",
			"parentId": "109671085446712957",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong/109671338167338486",
			"author": {
				"name": "Cory Birdsong",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@cbirdsong",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/543/551/045/998/536/original/e10f042a7b2e4a2e.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-11T15:43:35.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@bkardell\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bkardell</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mstdn.ca/@AmeliasBrain\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>AmeliasBrain</span></a></span> </p><p>I think that rating a movie doesn’t go in your diary so you can backfill or adjust ratings without it assuming you just watched the movie, which generates an item in your followers’ feed and affects your monthly/yearly watch stats.</p><p>If you want it to be recorded in your diary, you have log it, which also prompts you to add a rating. </p><p>(I don’t get “like” either, but I guess maybe it’s for people who get analysis paralysis trying to rate things on a scale 🤷)</p>",
